paceIndex stores the sealed source inventory and input separately from its immutable original declaration/navigation inventory and any independently supplied completed world. Current readonly candidate/assistance selection uses the surviving conditional source slot while mapping to the canonical original declaration, so a moved New candidate does not revive Old or Removed. Settlement dependency records retain current slot, original factory geometry, lineage, unknown-operation premises and obligations; reindex/removal/slot reuse changes or withdraws that advice. Missing/foreign/configuration-drifted retained input withholds candidates even when original declarations remain available, and actual unavailable factory vocabulary creates no declaration. Canonical original source navigation and current conditional candidate advice remain distinct from runtime object allocation, installed/current Native tables, entered lookup/frame, execution and edit authority. Core class-command and method candidate consumers retain authentic source_constructor_call_at at each original call horizon rather than replace earlier applicability with the final inventory. A boxed genuine source call keeps its own obligations and captured effective selector; a captured selector does not create a cursor operand. Workspace unresolved class-name advice selects current publication slots while canonical original MRO/declaration records remain independent. SourceClass::matches_source_declaration is only the canonical original occurrence join used by source_class and publication candidates. A positive Native name-input domain is required before these consumers intercept a call; Logical and hosted factory source receipts cannot become Native method queries or block separately admitted Logical advice.",
